      <div itemprop="text">
        <p>Kobo Plus borrowed books cannot be read directly on Kindle devices because the EPUB files are protected by Adobe DRM and tied to your Kobo account. If you purchase the Harry Potter ebooks outright from the Kobo store, you can download the EPUB files, use Calibre to convert them, and transfer them to your Kindle. However, Kobo Plus subscription borrows (rentals) are locked to the Kobo ecosystem — Amazon does not support Adobe DRM EPUB files on Kindle hardware.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
